\begin{theorem}[Conditional Phenomenological Closure]\label{thm:closure}
A declared separated, detected pair has a non-empty positive image and the unanchored lower bound $\max_i r(\Phi(z_i))\geq C\epsilon/2$. Its finite positive image has a minimal member; uniqueness requires comparability. If one endpoint is null, the other is the unique positive witness image, with relative gap and null distance at least $C\epsilon$. Temporal stability, global minimal positivity, and physical CCR realizability are not consequences.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
Combine Theorem~\ref{thm:instability}, Theorem~\ref{thm:minimal}, Corollary~\ref{cor:intensity} and the anchored bound of Theorem~\ref{thm:bound}. Each conclusion retains its stated hypotheses.
\end{proof}

