\subsection{Artifact Contract for Prediction Claims}
Every prediction claim should be backed by a finite evidence bundle:
\[
\mathcal{B}=(\mathcal{M},\mathcal{P},\mathcal{J},\mathcal{R},\mathcal{A}),
\]
where $\mathcal{M}$ is the manifest set, $\mathcal{P}$ the observation packet set,
$\mathcal{J}$ the executable evaluator code and threshold records, $\mathcal{R}$ the run/exclusion
ledger, and $\mathcal{A}$ the executable analysis scripts. The bundle is part of the claim
surface. A table without the bundle is a summary, not independently checkable
evidence.

\begin{criterion}[Bundle Sufficiency]
For any status stronger than \Status{STILL\_AMBIGUOUS}, the evidence bundle must
allow an evaluator to reconstruct the reported verdicts from sealed inputs without
manual row selection.
\end{criterion}

\begin{criterion}[Externalization Readiness]
A prediction family is ready for external evaluation only when its bundle,
thresholds, exclusions, and decision rules are exportable without access to live
generator state or informal operator knowledge.
\end{criterion}

