\subsection{Binding Predictions to an External Biological Interface}
Each proposed external falsifier must instantiate the experimental interface contract of Paper IV: population and independent unit, preparation, target/sham/disconnection/restoration operators, measured channels and units, frozen blinded decoder, calibrated error, matched information/cost, and identifying causal assumptions. A biological preparation is a candidate realization of the abstract model, not an automatic instance of its invariants. A missing realization or observation map leaves the prediction unevaluable on that preparation.

For a directional predicted margin $\eta$, preregister the score, measurement headroom and multiplicity before data. Under the independent-block contract, the lower rejection boundary is $\eta-t_n-2Le$, with the false-rejection and power statements of Paper IV. Distinguish a valid adverse contrast from invalid sham matching, sensor dropout, leakage or an unidentified intervention. Equal recorded laws for candidate and rival make separation impossible on that interface. No simulation or terminology can remove that identification obstruction. This is a falsation specification, not an executed biological campaign; external support remains uncertified.

\subsection{Constructive Indexed and Metric-Sector Discriminators}
The native asymmetric infinite plant of Papers V, VII and VIII supplies a
joint instrumented certificate rather than seven disconnected score flags.
Its new predictions are conditional on its equations and comparison grammar:
paired valuation pulses give responses $4385/262144$ and $4321/262144$;
rate symmetrization makes their signed contrast zero. Ownership collapse,
privileged-history fracture and an exact added clone destroy the corresponding
conjunctive margins. The reserved three-port task has weak loss $14/15$ and
native loss $3/16$ in its common three-operation language; an unrestricted
same-cost emulator removes that advantage. These are analytic/synthetic
discriminators, not measurements from a physical or biological submission.

Paper I's wedge result is likewise sector-specific: fixing positive factor
diameters and bi-Lipschitz constants gives a positive Hausdorff gap and a
half-gap perturbation radius. Letting a factor shrink or the lower Lipschitz
constant vanish defeats the conclusion. Its protected/damage actuation
contrast uses a stated operational cost model; a real cheap clamp in the
same sector would preclude the strict resistance threshold. No experimental
claim may combine those two incompatible premises or transfer the radius to
arbitrary homeomorphisms. Fresh external tests must identify these observation,
control, energy and grammar assumptions through the Paper IV interface.

\section{Conclusion}
The canon now has a prediction layer and a failure-mode ledger with explicit discriminators, explicit weakening conditions, and explicit support classes.

The current internal picture is sharp enough to summarize without inflation. The complexity/connectivity insufficiency claim has robust internal support. Substrate-preserved class membership and biological non-primacy now have robust support with localized caveats. Approximate stability is provisionally supported with a localized threshold caveat. Boundary-sensitive stress of existence and rupture now has robust support with localized caveats under convergent internal probe families and a more independent judge path. All of this nevertheless remains internal-only.

This remains an internal prediction-and-falsation specification. It does not upgrade the formal framework to external validation, theorem closure beyond the upstream papers, or unconditional empirical certification.

