$q=b_4=1$, $u=-\lambda\ell(\bar z)/4$, $v=0$ and let $c_I$ be the
first-query clearance from the predeclared kernel phase zero. The ordinary
sham pads the second step. Put $d_I=3/2048$ and define the
two candidate weights by
\[
 q=\bigl((1+\operatorname{clip}(c_I/d_I))/2,
         (1-\operatorname{clip}(c_I/d_I))/2\bigr),
\]
where clipping is to $[-1,1]$. This is a calibrated score rule, not a claim
of posterior probability. Include the common signed port/prefix renamings,
