Its score is the minimum of these two temporal correlations, so an intermediate
misbinding is not erased by endpoint recovery. The two continuity candidates are the retained indexed line
and this matched alternative; their scores enter the canonical estimator
with $s_C=1$. An exact added clone is a distinct comparison control.

For P and R use independent, separately labelled balanced sign-cube populations
in the reserved task of Lemma~\ref{lem:indexed-causal-closure-loss}, on Hilbert
coordinates 4 and 5 respectively. Predictions are fixed before their outcomes;
no empirical fit to one population supplies an uncharged feature to the other.
The five-coordinate intervention profile never enters either predictor.
Use $s_P=313/240$ and $s_R=1$ in the existing normalized estimators.

For V start from the same sham fixed point and use a pulse of amplitude
$a_1=1/2$ on the indexed port or its partner, followed by sham, with
$q=u=0$. The response is the sum of squared Hilbert deviations from the
corresponding common sham at times 1 and 2. Both pulses have identical
