\[
\text{formalized}
\not\Rightarrow
\text{implemented}
\not\Rightarrow
\text{admissible}
\not\Rightarrow
\text{phenomenality simpliciter}.
\]
Each step requires explicit additional verification: formalization corresponds to Tier~B0 specification; implementation to the respective realization tier; admissibility to joint comparator, intervention, gate, and governance closure; and phenomenality simpliciter lies wholly outside the bridge program.

