Paper 10 sits on a strict separation between mathematical formalization and empirical execution:

\begin{itemize}
\item BaseCore and Papers I--IX supply mathematical definitions, structural obstructions, finite constructive certificates, and conditional falsification criteria.
\item The external adjudication protocol defined in Paper 10 specifies how future empirical campaigns would be preregistered, blinded, audited, and judged.
\item Inclusion of this protocol monograph in the collected theoretical framework supplies zero execution-era human data and establishes no empirical support.
\item Tiers P0 through P7 specify procedural, freeze, rehearsal, and controlled-opening conditions that remain non-evidential until executed independently with external participants.
\end{itemize}

Therefore publication within the theoretical corpus cannot be substituted for empirical adjudication,
and protocol completeness cannot be substituted for experimental closure.

\section{Lineage and Provenance Semantics}

Tiers P3 and P4 enforce a strict authority hierarchy; every admissible record must distinguish among:

\begin{enumerate}
\item public theoretical framework authority,
\item local protocol specification authority,
\item frozen preregistration authority,
\item reviewer-package authority,
\item adjudicator-package authority, and
\item execution-era evidence authority.
\end{enumerate}

Archived records whose lineage reflects prior protocol snapshots are preserved intact for provenance; live specification bindings are updated explicitly without altering historical records retroactively.

