\section{External Interface Admission Before Biological Adjudication}
The experimental interface contract in Paper IV is an admission prerequisite, not a new support label. An external submission supplies its population/preparation, independent blocks, sensory/motor and measurement maps, units and noise calibration, matched sham, causal disconnection preserving observation, restoration control, frozen blinded decoder, rival information/cost and causal identification assumptions. Missing maps are recorded as insufficient evidence; invented biological observations are not admissible.

The forced-choice/abstention loss of this paper remains unchanged. It concerns labels and cannot replace the model-specific falsation contrast. For the latter, the Paper IV blockwise rule bounds false rejection by $\min(1,\alpha+\beta+p)$ only when the claimed audit failure probability is backed by a coupling to the specified blind reference design. An observed audit pass rate alone is insufficient. Calibration failure, leakage, dependence between purported units and off-target disconnection effects have separate status fields. A valid rejection bears on the realized model and its observation/causal contract; it does not refute an abstract theorem whose hypotheses have not been instantiated. Acceptance here supplies no empirical support until an actual independent submission satisfies the existing evidence and governance gates. External support remains uncertified.

\paragraph{Admission of the new constructive certificates.}
Paper VIII's native infinite-dimensional member proves nonemptiness of its
instrumented indexed class relative to a fully specified causal/computational
grammar. Paper I supplies metric-sector product gaps and a conditional
protected-actuator threshold. Neither result changes this adjudicator's
loss, coverage, blinding, leakage or external-evidence requirements. In a
submission using the indexed forecast, admit same-information/cost emulators
as an explicit sensitivity control; if they match the candidate, the raw
comparative margin is nonpositive. In a wedge submission, declare factor
diameters, distortion constants and actual energy calibration rather than
borrowing a mathematical actuator's units. Independent data, method review
and replication remain unexecuted unless a submission documents them;
\texttt{external\_support\_certified=false} remains the internal boundary.

