\item \texttt{\detokenize{phenomen}\allowbreak{}\detokenize{al_}\allowbreak{}\detokenize{bridge_}\allowbreak{}\detokenize{gate_}\allowbreak{}\detokenize{result}}
\item \texttt{\detokenize{phenomen}\allowbreak{}\detokenize{al_}\allowbreak{}\detokenize{bridge_}\allowbreak{}\detokenize{manifest}}
\end{enumerate}
These schemas correspond to aggregate run-level bridge projection, gate verdict, and lineage root. They are formally specified in the schema hierarchy but remain intentionally unpopulated until bridge comparator, intervention, and gate layers are executed. Their status is \emph{schema-bound, unpopulated, non-authoritative}.

