\section{Open Questions}

The following questions are deliberately left open because the present paper lacks the definitions or empirical evidence required to decide them.

\begin{enumerate}[leftmargin=1.5em]
\item Is $\Sigma1$ necessary for any plausible indexed continuity-and-control criterion class, or only for the bridge class $\Subbridge$ defined here?
\item Can $\Sigma1$ be derived from $\Iint+\Ileg$ under additional architectural hypotheses, such as decoder closure under self-targeted interventions?
\item Does a hierarchy of self-models $\Sigma^{(0)},\Sigma^{(1)},\dots$ produce a formal higher-order analogue, or does it merely add regress without new invariant content?
\item Is CCR strength $\MO=+\infty$ necessary for any non-weak version of $\Phiop$, or only sufficient for forced continuity?
\item Can full Paper 7 $\Subop$ be reduced to $\Cop+\Sigma1+\Lop$ plus a finite list of descriptor inequalities, or do ownership and privileged continuity require independent axioms?
\item Which runtime observables would distinguish genuine intervention commutation of $\Sigma$ from a stable but epiphenomenal self-model proxy?
\item What external experimental campaign could adjudicate whether internal-support certificates track any real-world subjecthood-relevant structure?
\item Are there finite systems that approximate $\Subbridge$ arbitrarily well while provably failing CCR, and if so what is the exact approximation boundary?
\item Can certified response classes non-triviality be certified without relying on a fixed decoder family, or is decoder dependence constitutive of $\Qop(S)$?
\item What, if anything, connects these structural predicates to ordinary moral or legal categories? This paper provides no such bridge.
\end{enumerate}

\subsection{A Complete Infinite-Dimensional Non-Entailment Witness}
\begin{corollary}[Global Self-Reference and Indexed Valuation Are Not Forced]\label{cor:infinite-cop-nonentailed}
The global Hilbert--prefix system of Paper V satisfies the complete six-predicate criterion in its declared model universe. Nevertheless it admits no global strict contraction $\Sigma:A\to A$ commuting exactly with every admitted intervention, and its matched exchange protocol gives zero valuation asymmetry as in Paper VIII. Thus neither that global self-reference requirement nor the seven-coordinate indexed class follows from $\Cop$ alone.
\end{corollary}
\begin{proof}
The support is complete and nonempty. A global strict contraction has a unique fixed point. Exact commutation makes every intervention preserve that point. But $D_{0,0,0}$ and $D_{1/4,0,0}$ force its phase to be respectively zero and one quarter, which is impossible. The separate involution exchanging the two Hilbert coordinate groups commutes with the controlled dynamics when inputs and references are exchanged, so every paired weighted response agrees and its valuation contrast is zero. Global criterion membership is proved in Paper V; the argument is not based only on local scores. Fibrewise or approximate self-reference remains a different condition.
\end{proof}

\begin{corollary}[Native Indexed Membership Does Not Force Exact Global Self-Reference]
\label{cor:native-indexed-selfreference-boundary}
The complete asymmetric native model of Papers V, VII and VIII realizes
$\Subfp(2)$ under its explicit causal grammar and positive thresholds.
It still has no global strict contraction on its complete support commuting
with every admissible control. Thus a nonempty indexed certificate class
does not remove the separate exact-global-self-reference obstruction.
\end{corollary}
\begin{proof}
The native construction supplies the full global six-predicate certificate,
all life and indexed continuity descriptors, seven positive coordinates and
strict loss over the entire declared weak closure. This is a completed
instrumented mathematical member, not a runtime or experiential promotion.
Its controls still contain $D_{0,0,0}$ and $D_{1/4,0,0}$. A global strict
contraction commuting with both would have a common fixed point, whose phase
would have to be both zero and one quarter. This is impossible. Fibrewise
contraction and bounded commutation defect remain separate, potentially
realizable requirements; no full bridge membership is inferred here.
\end{proof}

\section{Conclusion}

The bridge supplies conditional population-level directional sensitivity and a certified response quotient when its decoder-visible separation premises hold. Global exact commutation with a strict contraction is obstructed by incompatible fixed-point controls; the fibrewise bounded-defect variant has separate hypotheses. The symmetric infinite-dimensional criterion witness gives a concrete non-entailment example for global self-reference and, through the paired valuation protocol, for seven-coordinate indexed membership. The separate asymmetric native construction now realizes the full indexed class in its declared causal grammar; Corollary~\ref{cor:native-indexed-selfreference-boundary} shows that even this stronger certificate does not supply exact global self-reference. Neither construction supplies a phenomenal interpretation or empirical external support.

